committer Mizuki Hayashi <mizuki@kamiyo.ai> 1792224974 +0200

fix(v16): refuse fresh backing withdrawal from a lapsed bucket

withdraw_fresh_counterparty_backing_not_atomic never compared the bucket's
expiry with the current slot, so a provider could withdraw unliened
principal from a Fresh bucket at or past its expiry slot. Expiry forfeits
that principal to the junior pool, and validate_source_domain_ledger_current
already refuses the same state with Stale before a credit-rate read. In a
resolved market, withdrawing first left a haircut receipt paid 1 of 4
instead of 4 of 4.

Return Stale before any mutation when the bucket is Fresh and
expiry_slot <= current_slot. Other statuses keep their LockActive refusal.

The percolator-prog wrapper has refused this at its WithdrawBackingBucket
boundary since fe64fb71 (AUDIT-063), but the engine route itself was open,
so any other caller of the public API inherited the gap. The engine now
enforces it directly.

Fixes #240.
